\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sun of my soul , Thou Saviour dear,
\par It is not night if  Thou be near;
\par O may no earth- born cloud arise
\par To hide Thee from Thy servant's eyes!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When the soft dews of kindly sleep
\par My wearied eyelids gently steep,
\par Be my last thought: How sweet to rest
\par For ever on my Saviour's breast!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Abide with me from morn till eve,
\par For without Thee I cannot live;
\par Abide with me when night is nigh,
\par For without Thee I dare not die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If some poor wandering child of Thine
\par Have spurned to-day the voice divine,
\par Now, Lord, the gracious work begin;
\par Let him no more lie down in sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Watch by the sick; enrich the poor
\par With blessings from Thy boundless store,
\par Be every mourner's sleep to- night,
\par Like infant's slumbers, pure and light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Come near and bless us when we wake,
\par Ere through the world our way we take,
\par Till in the ocean of Thy love
\par We lose ourselves in heaven above.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

